  "raw_text": "Not necessarily. A 10% monthly sales decline alone doesn’t prove the campaign failed. You’d need context, including:\n\n- Sales trends before and after the campaign\n- A control group or comparable period without the campaign\n- Seasonality and broader market conditions\n- Changes in pricing, inventory, distribution, or competitors\n- Campaign goals beyond immediate sales, such as awareness or lead generation\n- Statistical uncertainty and whether the decline is meaningful\n- Return on ad spend and longer-term customer value\n\nThe campaign is more credibly judged by comparing actual results with a defined baseline or control and with its pre-set objectives.",
